Jahshaka patch 0066 — a cascaded cone march must CARRY THE CONE across the hop.

MEDIA-only patch (one Hlms piece: `Samples/Media/Hlms/Pbs/Any/Vct_piece_ps.any`).
THE PROCESS COST IS STATED RATHER THAN AVOIDED: Studio stages its media from the
SOURCE tree (cmake/IncludeOgre.cmake), so every tree must still reset its
ogre-next submodule and re-run `irisgl/scripts/build-ogre.sh` — no engine
recompile beyond the staging. It OVERLAPS patches 0021, 0033, 0045 and 0048 in
the same file, so a tree that already carries those hits `build-ogre.sh`'s
"Upstream changed the patched file" on a re-run: that is the documented
per-patch reverse-check blind spot and NOT an upstream change. The cure is the
recorded one — `git -C irisgl/thirdparty/ogre-next checkout -- . && git -C
irisgl/thirdparty/ogre-next clean -fd` and re-run the script.

WHY (Jahshaka lane SEAM-1, 2026-09-16, measured; PHOTON-E3 named the symptom).
On a 400 m slab lit by nothing but an ambient, with the camera-centred cascade
chain bound, the ambient a surface receives falls by a STEP at every cascade
face — one step per cascade, 1.15-1.24x each, travelling with the camera, and by
a factor of 1.9 from the far world to the eye. The single fitted volume has no
such face (1.007-1.029x). The step is the same RATIO under a flat ambient, a
hemisphere pair and the engine's analytic sky at noon and at 5 degrees, which is
what rules out a spherical-harmonic band mismatch: it is a pure multiplier on
the cone's ambient weight. PHOTON_SPEC tracks the accumulated loss as "the
cascade march residual (0.51x)"; patch 0033's own header table measured it as a
chain-length sweep, 1.00 / 0.75 / 0.56 / 0.51 for one to four cascades.

The continuation loop in `computeVctProbe` carries the exit POSITION, the colour
opacity and the mip across a hop. It does not carry the other two things a cone
IS, and each of them is one of the steps.

  (a) THE ESCAPE OPACITY IS RE-SEEDED FROM THE COLOUR OPACITY AT EVERY HOP.
      `voxelConeTraceDiff` opens with `float escapeAlpha = startingAlpha;`, and
      `startingAlpha` is the caller's `result.alpha`, not its
      `result.escapeAlpha`. Patch 0021 introduced `escapeAlpha` precisely
      because under anisotropic tracing the two legitimately differ — the axis
      textures are composited along their own axis, so a one-voxel-thick floor
      reads alpha 1 along +/-Y at every mip while the cone's real chance of
      escaping is a fraction of that — and 0021's header recorded this seeding
      as "a small approximation only that path pays". It is not small. Since
      `escapeAlpha <= alpha` always, every hop RAISES the escape opacity to the
      colour opacity, so the ambient weight the cone carries (`light.w`) loses a
      step per cascade, once per cascade, for exactly the pixels that are inside
      the most cascades. That is the staircase, and it is why the single volume
      — which never hops — does not have it.

  (b) THE CONE'S AGE IS RESET AT EVERY HOP, so it is re-born narrow.
      `dist` does two jobs at once: it POSITIONS the samples
      (`nextPosLS = posLS + dist * dirLS`) and it SIZES the cone
      (`diameter = 2 tan(theta) dist`, from which the mip follows). Positioning
      from the new cascade's entry point is right; SIZING from it is not — a
      cone's footprint is a function of how far it has come FROM THE SURFACE.
      The hand-off is arranged to happen exactly when the footprint reaches the
      next cascade's cell, so the reset looks harmless, but the restart's first
      diameter is `2 * 0.577 * cell = 1.154 cell` and from there the cone grows
      as though its apex sat at the entry point rather than at the surface: every
      hop re-anchors the apex about 0.87 cells behind where it belongs and the
      whole march through that cascade runs at a footprint that never matches
      the cone's true solid angle. The escape estimate is accumulated per
      sample, so a wrong footprint is a wrong escape.

THE FIX is to carry both. `VctResult` gains `travelled` — the distance from the
SURFACE, in the local-space units of the cascade the cone is currently in — and
the trace takes `startingEscapeAlpha` and `startingTravelled`. `dist` keeps its
positioning job unchanged; `diameter` is computed from `travelled`. At the hop
the caller hands over its own `result.escapeAlpha` and its `result.travelled`
converted into the next cascade's units by `dot( abs( dir ),
fromPreviousProbeToNext[j-1][0].xyz )` — the same directional scale upstream
already uses for `vctInvResolution`, and exactly the scale `fromVctProbeToNext`
applies to a position, because a length in one cascade's normalised box is a
length in the next one's box times the ratio of the box sizes.

THE FIRST CASCADE IS ARITHMETICALLY UNTOUCHED. The first call passes
`startingTravelled` 0 and the trace floors it at `vctInvResolution`, which is
what `dist` is initialised to, so `travelled == dist` for every step of a
single-volume march and every expression is the one it was. Measured, not
asserted: the default scene rendered with the chain OFF is sha256-IDENTICAL
between the two medias (7407fff2ded7f6462fb2ca3f23f11d292484b6395d56931922814132a25a5799),
and `gi.chain_face`'s single-volume readings are unchanged to four decimals
under all four ambients.

MEASURED (Jahshaka `gi.chain_face`, the 400 m slab, High, the +/-20 m reading;
the face ratio is the picture beyond the face over the picture inside it, and
1.000x is no face):

                         flat        hemisphere   sky-noon
    cascade 0 face   0.591 -> 1.000  0.604 -> 1.003  0.679 -> 1.086
    cascade 1 face   1.154 -> 0.821  1.157 -> 0.825  1.150 -> 0.833
    cascade 2 face   1.138 -> 1.000  1.140 -> 1.000  1.125 -> 1.000

As a profile across the slab (flat ambient), against the ambient a pixel outside
the chain receives: the ring nearest the eye went from 0.567x to 0.959x of it —
PHOTON_SPEC's 0.51x cascade march residual, measured at 0.96x. Four faces became
one, and the one that is left sits at the 128^3 -> 64^3 cell-size jump in the
tier's own cascade table (0.156 m to 0.469 m), not at a cascade hop: it is the
coarse cell over-occluding a 0.1 m slab through patch 0021's deliberately
conservative `min3` escape estimate, and it is a table question, not a march one.

NOT DONE HERE, and each was measured before it was dropped: terminating the
march on the escape opacity rather than the colour opacity is bit-identical in
every arm (the march never reaches alpha 0.95 in these scenes), and dropping
upstream's second `( 1.0 - result.alpha )` de-amplification of a cascade's
colour moves an interior hall by 0.6 % — neither earns a line.

THE SPECULAR WALK TAKES THE ESCAPE CARRY AND NOT THE AGE CARRY, and the
asymmetry is measured rather than assumed. The two marches hand over at
different places and weigh their escape with different estimates: the diffuse
trace exits at `cascadeMaxLod` — its footprint has grown to exactly the next
cascade's cell — and its ambient rides `escapeAlpha`, patch 0021's `min3` of the
axis composites, a deliberately conservative estimate of what the cone hit; the
specular trace runs to `maxLod = 11`, i.e. until it leaves the BOX, and its
ambient rides the raw `alpha`, the direction-weighted axis composite, which
over-states occlusion at a coarse mip (0021's whole finding). Carrying the true
age into the specular walk hands a cone that has crossed a whole cascade a
correspondingly wide footprint — right geometry fed to an opacity estimate that
is already too high. Measured on `gi.cascades` case 7 (a smooth metal plate
reflecting open space under a chain): the ambient in the reflection fell from
1.00 / 0.85 / 0.85 to 1.00 / 0.43 / 0.34 at one, two and four cascades. Passing
0 restores upstream's arithmetic exactly on that walk (the trace floors the age
at `vctInvResolution`, which is what `dist` starts at, so `travelled == dist` for
every step) and case 7 reads its pinned 1.00 / 0.85 / 0.85 again.
THE HONEST CURE FOR THE SPECULAR SIDE IS ITS OWN LANE: giving `specAlpha` the
same `min3` estimate the diffuse ambient already uses was built and measured here
— 1.00 / 0.88 / 0.87 under a chain, and better than the pin at every roughness
(0.35: 0.68 / 0.51 against 0.00 / 0.00; 0.55: 0.55 / 0.40 against 0.00 / 0.00) —
but it moves the SINGLE-VOLUME reflection as well, so it needs its own pictures
and its own gate, not a ride on this one.

UPSTREAM-REPORTABLE: (a) is Jahshaka's own since 0021 and is fixed here; (b) is
upstream's, and upstream's own `LightVctBounceInject_piece_cs.any` carries the
same reset (and, separately, still carries the `result.alpha += newRes.alpha`
opacity doubling that patch 0033 fixed on the pixel side).

